course: dictionary
lesson: 11061
title: Weeper and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A weeper is a person who weeps, which means someone who cries easily or often. Many words have more than one meaning, so read the clues around the word. Ask yourself who or what the word is describing.
explain: «Finders keepers, losers weepers» is a playground rhyme. Here the losers are the ones who cry, so weepers means children who weep when they lose something. The rhyme is a joke, not a rule: a lost thing still belongs to its owner, even if you found it.
explain: A weeper can also be a sad film or story that makes people cry, and people call it «a real weeper» or «weepie». In history, weepers were people paid to cry at funerals. Plants like the weeping willow have drooping branches. Same word, different clues.
fact: A weeper is a person who weeps, or cries easily or often.
fact: Informally, a weeper is a sad film or story that makes people cry; «weepie» means the same.
fact: In history, weepers were people paid to cry at funerals, or small statues of mourners on old tombs.
fact: The «weeping willow» is a tree with long branches that droop down.
fact: «Finders keepers, losers weepers» is a playground rhyme, not a rule.
exercise: In the rhyme «Finders keepers, losers weepers», what does weepers mean? | Rain clouds | *People who cry when they lose something | People who find lost things | Teachers
exercise: «She was a weeper, always crying at the smallest thing.» What does weeper mean here? | A paid mourner at a funeral | A tree with drooping branches | A dog that barks | *A person who cries easily or often
exercise: Your friend says the film was «a real weeper». What does she mean? | A film about trees | A film that is very funny | A film with no sound | *A very sad film that makes people cry
test: Which tree has long branches that droop down? | *Weeping willow | Weepie | Weeper | Mourner
test: In history, what were weepers? | Judges in a court | Children at school | *People paid to cry at funerals | Kings and queens
exam: Which sentence uses weeper to mean a sad film? | The weeper hung down over the pond | Weepers were people paid to cry | She is a weeper, always crying | *The new film is a real weeper, so bring tissues
